{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall not let a sorceress live</b>. Above, in connection with all those liable to capital punishment, it says \"shall surely be put to death\" (Exodus 14:16, 21:12) — the meaning being that he is liable to death, and there is a positive commandment upon us to put him to death, either from what is written \"you shall purge the evil from your midst\" (Deuteronomy 17:7), or from the verse itself that commands that he be put to death. But here it does not say 'a sorceress shall surely be put to death.' Instead, He was stricter concerning her, warning us with a negative commandment not to let her live. The reason is that because she is an impurity of HaShem that causes great confusion, and fools are drawn after her, He was stricter concerning her with a negative commandment. And so with all cases of widespread stumbling, as for example He said concerning the inciter: \"and you shall not spare and you shall not conceal him\" (Deuteronomy 13:9), and He said concerning the murderer: \"and you shall take no ransom for the life of a murderer who is wicked to die\" (Numbers 35:31)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:14:03.426506662Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}